---
import { Image, getImage } from 'astro:assets';
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import founderPhoto from '../assets/about/founder.jpg';
import channelPicture from '../assets/about/levine-tech-talks.jpg';
import { ADS_ENABLED, CONTACT_EMAIL, FOUNDER, GITHUB_URL, PROJECTS, YOUTUBE } from '../config';
import { getPosts } from '../lib/blog';

const posts = await getPosts();
const topicCount = new Set(posts.map((post) => post.data.topic)).size;

const shareImage = await getImage({ src: founderPhoto, width: 640, height: 640, format: 'jpg' });

const founderJsonLd = {
  '@type': 'Person',
  '@id': 'https://anyairdrop.com/about/#founder',
  name: FOUNDER.name,
  jobTitle: FOUNDER.title,
  url: 'https://anyairdrop.com/about/',
  image: new URL(shareImage.src, Astro.site).toString(),
  sameAs: [FOUNDER.linkedin, YOUTUBE.url, GITHUB_URL, ...PROJECTS.map((project) => project.url)],
  knowsAbout: FOUNDER.skills,
  worksFor: { '@id': 'https://anyairdrop.com/#organization' },
};

const facts = [
  { value: String(posts.length), label: `guides in ${topicCount} topics` },
  { value: 'Free', label: 'no account, no app' },
  { value: 'Open', label: 'source, MIT license' },
];
---

<Page
  title="About AnyAirDrop.com: Who Runs It, How It Works and Why"
  description="AnyAirDrop.com sends files between phones and computers over your Wi-Fi, in the browser. Meet the founder, see how the site is run and funded, and how your data is handled."
  heading="About AnyAirDrop.com"
  lead="AnyAirDrop.com sends files between iPhones, Android phones, Windows PCs, Macs and Linux computers over your Wi-Fi, right in the browser. No app, no account, no upload. This page says who runs it, how it works and how it is paid for."
  type="AboutPage"
  extraJsonLd={[founderJsonLd]}
>
  <ul class="facts" aria-label="At a glance">
    {
      facts.map((fact) => (
        <li>
          <span class="fact-value">{fact.value}</span>
          <span class="fact-label">{fact.label}</span>
        </li>
      ))
    }
  </ul>

  <h2>Who is behind it</h2>
  <div class="founder">
    <Image
      class="portrait"
      src={founderPhoto}
      alt={`${FOUNDER.name}, founder of AnyAirDrop.com, standing outdoors in a white shirt and sunglasses`}
      width={160}
      height={160}
      widths={[160, 320]}
      sizes="160px"
      loading="eager"
    />
    <div class="founder-body">
      <p class="founder-name">{FOUNDER.name}</p>
      <p class="founder-role">{FOUNDER.title} and publisher</p>
      <p>
        Hi, I’m {FOUNDER.name}. I’m a full-stack developer who likes fast, privacy-first web tools, and I design, build and
        look after AnyAirDrop.com myself. I am responsible for everything published here, and I read every message that
        comes in.
      </p>
      <ul class="links" aria-label={`${FOUNDER.name} online`}>
        <li><a href={YOUTUBE.url}>YouTube</a></li>
        <li><a href={FOUNDER.linkedin}>LinkedIn</a></li>
        <li><a href={GITHUB_URL}>GitHub</a></li>
      </ul>
      <ul class="skills" aria-label="Areas of work">
        {FOUNDER.skills.map((skill) => <li>{skill}</li>)}
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>Why it exists</h2>
  <p>
    Sending a photo or a video from one device to another is harder than it should be when the two devices come from
    different companies. AnyAirDrop.com makes it one tap: open the page on both devices, tap the other one, and the files go
    straight across. The <a href="/blog/">blog</a> grew out of the questions people have while using it, and now has
    {posts.length} guides on Wi-Fi, routers, phone modems and local file transfer.
  </p>

  <h2>Also on YouTube</h2>
  <p>
    I am also the owner of the YouTube channel <strong>{YOUTUBE.name}</strong>, an educational tech channel with
    step-by-step fixes and how-tos for Windows, games, streaming and hardware problems. It has more than 15,000 subscribers
    and over 100 videos, and several of its tutorials have each passed 400,000 views. The same approach goes into the guides
    on this site: explain the problem plainly, show the steps, and say what to check when they do not work.
  </p>
  <a class="channel" href={YOUTUBE.url}>
    <Image class="channel-picture" src={channelPicture} alt="" width={64} height={64} widths={[64, 128]} sizes="64px" />
    <span class="channel-text">
      <span class="channel-name">{YOUTUBE.name}</span>
      <span class="channel-handle">{YOUTUBE.handle} on YouTube</span>
    </span>
    <span class="channel-cta">Watch the channel <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></span>
  </a>

  <h2>How it works</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Device to device, encrypted.</strong> Your browser connects directly to the other browser and sends the file. It
      never passes through our server and is never stored. If a network blocks direct connections, an encrypted relay can
      carry the transfer, and the page tells you when that is happening.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Finding each other.</strong> Devices on the same Wi-Fi appear by themselves. Otherwise, type a six-digit code,
      scan a QR code, or use trusted devices that find each other every time.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>What our server sees.</strong> It only introduces devices: a random or chosen device name, the kind of device and
      browser, and a hashed network match, pairing code or trusted-device key. It never sees your files or their names and
      keeps no user database. Hosts keep standard technical logs, as on any website. The
      <a href="/privacy/">privacy page</a> has the full detail.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How the site is run and paid for</h2>
  {
    ADS_ENABLED ? (
      <p>
        AnyAirDrop.com is free to use. It is paid for by ads from Google AdSense that appear on the guides. They never appear
        on the transfer tool, they are kept visually separate from the articles, and they never change what a guide says.
        Nobody can pay to have a guide written, altered or removed.
      </p>
    ) : (
      <p>
        AnyAirDrop.com is free to use and currently shows no ads. If advertising is ever added, it will appear on the guides
        only, never on the transfer tool, and it will be described on the <a href="/privacy/">privacy page</a> and in the
        editorial policy. Nobody can pay to have a guide written, altered or removed.
      </p>
    )
  }

  <h2>How the guides are made</h2>
  <p>
    Every guide is built from primary sources, lists them at the bottom, and labels theoretical numbers as theoretical. Some
    are drafted with AI writing tools, and I review and take responsibility for what is published. The
    <a href="/editorial-policy/">editorial policy</a> explains the process and how to report a mistake.
  </p>

  <h2>More projects by {FOUNDER.name}</h2>
  <ul>
    {
      PROJECTS.map((project) => (
        <li>
          <a href={project.url}>{project.name}</a>: {project.summary}
        </li>
      ))
    }
  </ul>

  <h2>Independent and open source</h2>
  <p>
    AnyAirDrop.com is not affiliated with, endorsed by or sponsored by Apple Inc. or any other device maker. The code is open
    source under the MIT license: <a href={GITHUB_URL}>AnyAirDrop on GitHub</a>. See the <a href="/terms/">terms of use</a> for
    the ground rules.
  </p>

  <h2>Tell me what to improve</h2>
  <p>
    This site gets better through feedback, and I want to hear yours: something broken, something confusing, a guide that
    got a fact wrong, or a topic you would like explained. Write to
    <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>, open an issue on <a href={`${GITHUB_URL}/issues`}>GitHub</a>, or
    use the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>. I usually reply within 48 hours.
  </p>
</Page>

<style>
  .facts {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    margin: var(--space-4) 0 0;
    padding: 0 !important;
    list-style: none;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-line);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-line);
  }

  .facts li {
    margin: 0 !important;
    padding: var(--space-3) var(--space-3) var(--space-3) 0;
  }

  .facts li + li {
    padding-left: var(--space-3);
    border-left: 1px solid var(--color-line);
  }

  .fact-value {
    display: block;
    font-size: 28px;
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 1.1;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }

  .fact-label {
    display: block;
    margin-top: 4px;
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 1.4;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }

  .founder {
    display: flex;
    gap: var(--space-4);
    align-items: flex-start;
    margin-top: var(--space-2);
    padding: var(--space-4);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-line);
    border-radius: 16px;
    background: var(--color-surface);
  }

  .founder :global(.portrait) {
    flex: none;
    width: 160px;
    height: 160px;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-line);
    border-radius: 16px;
    object-fit: cover;
    object-position: center top;
  }

  .founder-body {
    min-width: 0;
  }

  .founder-body :global(p) {
    margin-top: 6px;
  }

  .founder-name {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 22px !important;
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 1.3 !important;
  }

  .founder-role {
    margin-top: 0;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-size: 14px !important;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .links,
  .skills {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 8px;
    margin: var(--space-2) 0 0;
    padding: 0 !important;
    list-style: none;
  }

  .links li {
    margin: 0 !important;
  }

  .links a {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    min-height: 40px;
    padding: 0 16px;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-line-strong);
    border-radius: var(--radius-button);
    font-size: 15px;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .links a:hover {
    border-color: var(--color-link);
  }

  .skills li {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 4px 12px;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-line);
    border-radius: 999px;
    font-size: 14px !important;
    line-height: 1.4 !important;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }

  .skills li + li {
    margin-top: 0 !important;
  }

  .channel {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-3);
    margin-top: var(--space-3);
    padding: var(--space-3);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-line);
    border-radius: 16px;
    background: var(--color-surface);
    color: var(--color-text);
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: border-color var(--dur-color) ease;
  }

  .channel:hover {
    border-color: var(--color-link);
  }

  .channel :global(.channel-picture) {
    flex: none;
    width: 64px;
    height: 64px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    object-fit: cover;
  }

  .channel-text {
    flex: 1;
    min-width: 0;
  }

  .channel-name,
  .channel-handle {
    display: block;
  }

  .channel-name {
    font-size: 19px;
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  .channel-handle {
    font-size: 15px;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }

  .channel-cta {
    flex: none;
    font-size: 15px;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--color-link);
  }

  @media (max-width: 560px) {
    .facts li {
      padding-right: var(--space-2);
    }

    .facts li + li {
      padding-left: var(--space-2);
    }

    .fact-value {
      font-size: 22px;
    }

    .fact-label {
      font-size: 13px;
    }

    .founder {
      flex-direction: column;
      padding: var(--space-3);
    }

    .channel {
      flex-wrap: wrap;
    }

    .channel-cta {
      width: 100%;
    }
  }
</style>
